      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T18:17:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The unit test cases are to show the unsafeness of the current code pattern.\n- `bind_front(\u0026Self::cb, this, shared_from_this())`\nand it is directly replaced by \n- `bind_front(\u0026Self::cb, shared_from_this())`.\n\nThis is more like syntax issue for the safe usage.\n\n\nLooking at https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/functional/bind_front,\nstd::bind_front() manual says \n```\ntemplate\u003c class F, class... Args \u003e\nconstexpr /* unspecified */ bind_front( F\u0026\u0026 f, Args\u0026\u0026... args );\n```\n\nNotes\n....\nAs described in std::invoke, when invoking a pointer to non-static member function or pointer to non-static data member, the first argument has to be a reference or pointer (including, possibly, smart pointer such as std::shared_ptr and std::unique_ptr) to an object whose member will be accessed.\n...\n\nSo, \nI\u0027m not sure whether we need the test for any of those, other than making sure it compiles.",
      "parentUuid": "4c04bedd_6cb4a406",
      "revId": "42f281e24fb72ab8e9652470f1fee3468142c950",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
